WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.060
Good morning Hank, it's Sunday.

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.600
So your video about the thirteen severed hands of Star Wars kind of blew my mind with its brilliance.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.900
By the way Nerdfighters, if you haven't seen it, you should. Link in the thingy.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.200
And when I was watching you showcase your masterful knowledge of the Star Wars universe,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.040
I started to think, like, I don't even know half of the severed hands of Star Wars.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.720
Maybe I'm not even a nerd?

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.580
Well Hank, as you can imagine, the thought that I wasn't a nerd was duly horrifying.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.800
But then I remembered that I had memorized all the known last words of American presidents.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.020
[Coughs, pops, and groans]

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.860
George Washington: "Tis well."

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.600
John Adams: "It is the glorious 4th of July. It is a great day. It is a good day."

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.980
And then he fell asleep and he woke up later and said, "Thomas Jefferson still survives."

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.040
Which wasn't true. Thomas Jefferson had died earlier that same day, July 4th, 1826.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.940
His last words were, "Is it the 4th?"

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.720
Actually, those weren't his last words. Those would have been great last words,

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.960
but then he said, "I resign my spirit to God and my daughter to my country."

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.900
At which point, his daughter was presumably like, "Dude, you don't own me. You can't resign me to anybody."

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.060
"I mean, like, geez, Dad. Do you believe that human beings can own other human beings?"

00:00:59.180 --> 00:00:59.680
Oh.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.280
Right, you do.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.300
James Madison: "I always talk better lying down."

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.980
James Monroe, speaking about James Madison, "I regret that I should ever leave this world

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.560
without again beholding him."

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.320
John Quincy Adams: "This is the last of the Earth. I am content."

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.060
Andrew Jackson: "Be good children, all of you, and strive to be ready when the change comes."

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.420
No mention of which change.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.420
Martin Van Buren: "There is but one reliance."

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.340
William Henry Harrison: "I wish you to understand the true principles of government.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.900
I ask them to be carried out. I ask nothing more."

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.300
John Tyler: "Doctor, I am going. Perhaps it is best."

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.280
James K. Polk, whose last words would be good last words for me too:

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.640
"I love you Sarah. I love you for all eternity."

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.040
Zachary Taylor: "I regret nothing, but I am sorry that I'm about to leave my friends."

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.780
The under appreciated Millard Fillmore, after drinking a spoonful of soup, famously said:

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.500
"The nourishment is palatable."

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.380
Franklin Pierce, tragically unknown.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.440
James Buchanan, seemingly aware of the fact that history would judge him

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.240
on of the worst presidents ever, said:

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.080
"I shall carry to my grave the consciousness that at least I meant well for my country.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.240
Oh, Lord God, as thou wilt."

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.360
Abraham Lincoln said: "Either it doesn't really matter or they won't think anything of it,"

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.460
as he was trying to convince his wife that they shouldn't be embarrassed about holding hands in public.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.000
Andrew Johnson: "I need no doctor. I can overcome my own trouble."

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:14.440
Or not.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.300
Ulysses S. Grant: "Water."

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.520
Rutherford B. Hayes: "I know I am going where Lucy is."

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.920
James Garfield: "Swain, can you stop this? Oh, Swain."

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:27.060
Swain was Garfield's chief-of-staff, but it occurs to me that Swain would be a pretty good substitute for dang.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.500
Like, aw swainit, I stubbed my toe.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.980
Chester A. Arthur: Unknown.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.140
Grover Cleveland: "I have tried so hard to do right."

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.180
Benjamin Harrison: "Doctor! My lungs!"

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.060
When William McKinley's wife said, "I want to go too," McKinley answered:

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.360
"We are all going."

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.440
Teddy Roosevelt: "Put out the light."

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.240
William Howard Taft's last words are unknown, but Woodrow Wilson's were:

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.900
"I'm a broken piece of machinery. When the machine is broken. I am ready."

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.320
Warren Harding: "That's good. Go on. Read some more."

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.640
Calvin Coolidge: "Good morning, Robert."

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.380
So, off topic, but Calvin Coolidge was famous for never saying anything,

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:04.440
and one time this woman comes up to him and she says, "So, my friend bet me that I couldn't get

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.740
more than two words out of you," at which point Calvin Coolidge says, "You lose."

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.140
Herbert Hoover: "Levi Strauss was one of my best friends."

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:15.060
Franklin Roosevelt: "I have a terrific pain in my head."

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.660
Harry Truman: Unknown.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:19.340
Dwight Eisenhower: "I'm ready to go, God. Take me."

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.920
John F. Kennedy, after being told that Dallas loved him, said:

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.320
"That's very obvious."

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.660
Lyndon Johnson's last words were, "Send Mike immediately."

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.920
Neither Nixon nor Reagan's last words were recorded.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.640
All other presidents are currently alive. I did it, Hank!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.020
You'll see me on Tuesday!

